BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Diwali / Deepavali [verify] / दीपावली [सत्य
 ापित करें]
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261109
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261110
DTSTAMP:20261103T043905Z
UID:diwali-2026-11-09@dharmasetu
CATEGORIES:festivals
DESCRIPTION:Why: light the home when the moon is dark — invite prosperit
 y\, kinship and clarity after the ancestral fortnight.\n\nStory: Diwali (D
 eepavali) on the amavasya of Ashvina (amanta) / Kartika lights lamps for R
 ama's return and Lakshmi's grace in the darkest new-moon night.\nSource: R
 amayana return narrative\; Padma Purana Lakshmi strands\nWhy: light the ho
 me when the moon is dark — invite prosperity\, kinship and clarity after
  the ancestral fortnight.\nModern angle: Light\, gathering and gift ritual
 s support mood and social ties in dark season\; cultural/psychological wit
 h seasonal-affect context.\nEvidence: Cultural/psychological\nMore: https:
 //saumya-sharma.github.io/dharmasetu/prototype/reasoning.html#calendar-lun
 isolar\nLocation basis: New Delhi. City-specific timing coming later.\n\n
 —\nदीपावली [सत्यापित करें]\nदी
 पावली आश्विन अमावस्या (अमान
 ्त) / कार्तिक — सबसे अँधेरी अम
 ावस्या पर राम की वापसी और लक
 ्ष्मी की कृपा के दीप।\nकारण: च
 ंद्र के अँधेरे में घर जलाएँ 
 — पितृ पक्ष के बाद समृद्धि\, र
 िश्ते और स्पष्टता का निमंत्
 रण।
LOCATION:New Delhi\, India (reference)
